<title>GERMANY: West German Mar industry output rises 0.1 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>West German Mar industry output rises 0.1 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Mar 97     Feb 97     Mar 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +0.1	 +1.1(+0.9) +2.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +3.2	 +5.3(+5.4) -2.4</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		97.0	 96.9(97.0) 94.0</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Mar 97		  Feb 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     82.6	 -3.8     85.9	 +0.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   96.8	 -0.2     97.0	 +0.9</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods  101.1	 -0.6     101.7	+3.2</p>
<p>	Capital goods     94.2	 -3.2     97.3	 -1.2</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 88.7	 +5.8     83.8	 -0.2</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    94.7	 +2.8     92.1	 -0.8</p>
<p> Energy output	   106.1	 +2.3    103.7	 -7.5</p>
<p> Construction	     96.2	 +3.0     93.4	+13.6</p>
<p>Two month comparison Mar-Feb 97 with Dec 96-Jan 97:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    +1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Mar-Feb 97 with Mar-Feb 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +2.0</p>
<p> Mining				    -4.7</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +1.9</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods     +4.4</p>
<p>		Capital goods	    +0.8</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	-0.2</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	   -1.4</p>
<p> Energy output			   -3.3</p>
<p> Construction			   +12.8</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
</text>
